This is a proof-of-concept setup of White Rabbit which utilizes the Fractional PLLs on an AMD Ultrascale+ FPGA
according to XAPP1276. Only a commonly available ZCU102 board is needed, without any external PLLs. SFP2 is being used
for 1G ethernet IO and upstream connectivity.

A custom FSBL build is needed to de-tune the MGT-Si570 clock chip on the board to precisely 124975605 Hz (see fsbl.patch).

To build a Vivado project and synthesize the bitstream follow these steps:

$ hdlmake
$ make files.tcl
$ vivado -mode tcl -source zcu102.tcl
